# Linux user service only: systemctl --user, never a rootful system service.
# Install binary at ~/.local/bin/pvisor-daemon and unit at
# ~/.config/systemd/user/pvisor-daemon.service. Copy this file to
# ~/.config/pvisor/daemon.env (chmod 600) and replace the empty key before starting.
# Use a strong random API key of at least 32 bytes, e.g. openssl rand -hex 32.
# This environment variable is distinct from the HTTP OPEN-SANDBOX-API-KEY header.
OPEN_SANDBOX_API_KEY=
# Must be an absolute path to a trusted rootless Podman executable.
PVISOR_DAEMON_PODMAN=/usr/bin/podman
PVISOR_DAEMON_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8080
PVISOR_DAEMON_MAX_SANDBOXES=32
PVISOR_DAEMON_CPU_MILLIS=4000
PVISOR_DAEMON_MEMORY_BYTES=8589934592
# Requires rootless Podman, cgroup v2 and delegated CPU/memory/PID controllers.
# Delegate= is a request, not proof that the host/user manager grants controllers;
# startup validates the runtime and fails closed when requirements are missing.
# Load prepared images into this same user's Podman store; pull=never.
# ENTRYPOINT must supervise workload argv and real OpenSandbox 1.1.0 execd/egress
# services on ports 44772/18080, initialize them, forward signals and reap children.
# Stock distro images are insufficient. Upstream default iptables-based egress
# cannot run unchanged with cap-drop=ALL: a capability-free service is required.
# No end-to-end prepared image recipe has been validated. No VM/stage/apply or
# network-policy enforcement is provided; unsupported options are rejected.
# Published loopback ports may be accessible to other local users. Protect guest
# service authentication and do not treat this as untrusted multi-user isolation.
# Keep loopback binding with this unit. External/wildcard listeners require TLS
# at a trusted proxy and an explicit --public-endpoint (host:port) unit override.
# State and native sandboxes intentionally survive restarts; never delete the
# state directory as a cleanup shortcut. TTL cleanup is best effort while running.
